<!-- SECTION 4: WHO CAN FILE -->
<section class="content-section" id="who-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">How to Respond - Step by Step</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Read notice carefully. Identify specific defect and deadline (15 days from notice date).</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Login to incometax.gov.in → Pending Actions → e-Proceedings → View notice.</p><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Choose response: <strong>Agree</strong> (defect is genuine, will rectify) or <strong>Disagree</strong> (return is correct, provide explanation).</p><p><strong>Step 4:</strong> If Agree: prepare corrected JSON using offline utility. Fix the defect. Pay additional tax if any via Challan 280.</p><p><strong>Step 5:</strong> Upload corrected JSON via e-Proceedings → Submit Response → Agree → Upload.</p><p><strong>Step 6:</strong> <strong>e-Verify</strong> the corrected return (Aadhaar OTP, net banking). Without verification, response is incomplete.</p><p><strong>Step 7:</strong> Track status until CPC updates to "Processed" or "No further action." Patron tracks until confirmation.</p>

            </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

